{:edb/db-before-t 2389 :edb/db-after-t 2390 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535702 50 #inst "2026-10-09T05:32:08.965Z" 13194139535702 true] [17592186198306 1020 #edb/ref 17592186362164 13194139535702 true] [17592186198319 1020 #edb/ref 17592186362150 13194139535702 true] [17592186198319 1020 #edb/ref 17592186362157 13194139535702 true] [17592186198521 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535702 true] [17592186198521 1100 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨z+y,\\,2y+z,\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=x-y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$" 13194139535702 true] [17592186198521 1100 "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$∬_(S)⟨z + y, 2y + z, xy⟩ \\cdot dS$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z = x - y$ for $0 \\le x \\le 1$ and $0 \\le y \\le 2$." 13194139535702 false] [17592186198521 1145 "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x-y)=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x-y)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨z+y,\\,2y+z,\\,xy⟩{|}_{z=x-y} \\\\  & =⟨(x-y)+y,\\,2y+(x-y),\\,xy⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{{x}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{x+y}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{xy}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z+y,\\,2y+z,\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(x)\\cdot 1-(x+y)\\cdot (-1)+xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-x+x+y+xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y+xy)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(y+xy)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[2x+{x}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(2(1)+{1}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535702 true] [17592186198542 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535702 true] [17592186198542 1100 "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=-x-y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" 13194139535702 true] [17592186198542 1100 "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$F(x, y, z) = ⟨e^{x}, e^{y}, z + 1⟩$,\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z =-x - y$ for $0 \\le x \\le 1$ and $0 \\le y \\le 1$." 13194139535702 false] [17592186198542 1145 "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-x-y)=-1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-x-y)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩{|}_{z=-x-y} \\\\  & =⟨{{{e}^{x}}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{{e}^{y}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{1-x-y}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{e}^{x},\\,{e}^{y},\\,z+1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-({e}^{x})\\cdot (-1)-({e}^{y})\\cdot (-1)+1-x-y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({e}^{x}+{e}^{y}+1-x-y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}+{e}^{y}+1-x-y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{e}^{x}y+{e}^{y}+y-xy-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}+e+1-x-\\frac{1}{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}-x-\\frac{1}{2}+e)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{e}^{x}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{x}{2}+ex]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =e-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}+e-1 \\\\  & =2e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362150 1017 #edb/ref 17592186362151 13194139535702 true] [17592186362150 1089 "q-161446" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362150 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535702 true] [17592186362150 1100 "For a surface $S$ given by $x=k(y,z)$ for $(y,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(P+\\frac{∂k}{∂y}-R\\frac{∂k}{})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362150 1113 #uuid "1b125418-463d-5d64-af0c-e0bb9a3a435d" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362150 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $x=k(y,z),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(y,z)=⟨k(y,z),\\,y,\\,z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂k}{∂z},\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂k}{∂y} & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{∂k}{∂z} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨1,\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂z}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂z}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(P+(-Q\\,)\\frac{∂k}{∂y}-R\\frac{∂k}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362152 13194139535702 true] [17592186362151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362153 13194139535702 true] [17592186362151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362154 13194139535702 true] [17592186362151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362155 13194139535702 true] [17592186362151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362156 13194139535702 true] [17592186362151 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535702 true] [17592186362151 1041 "selection" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362151 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362156 13194139535702 true] [17592186362151 1110 #uuid "295d3669-0b18-50cf-bcb3-1701ccc4eef7" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362152 1034 "$-R$ and $∂z$" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535702 true] [17592186362152 1111 #uuid "b1158736-1de5-5fbf-b48d-af048d0836ef" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362153 1034 "$-Q$ and $∂x$" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362153 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535702 true] [17592186362153 1111 #uuid "720e5c72-156a-529a-b954-0fadefeedcdc" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362154 1034 "$Q$ and $∂z$" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535702 true] [17592186362154 1111 #uuid "5e51c96c-bd01-54a2-87bb-25a5adc42bef" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362155 1034 "$Q$ and $∂x$" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535702 true] [17592186362155 1111 #uuid "c3f83a6d-f3dd-5130-aa17-a33405289612" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362156 1034 "$-Q$ and $∂z$" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362156 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535702 true] [17592186362156 1111 #uuid "f2811914-6f70-56dd-841f-80b6402cbcf0" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362157 1017 #edb/ref 17592186362158 13194139535702 true] [17592186362157 1089 "q-161457" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362157 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535702 true] [17592186362157 1100 "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{}{∂x}-\\frac{∂g}{}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362157 1113 #uuid "417f7e3b-659c-5f7d-913c-decf384148f3" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362157 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $z=g(x,y),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,g(x,y)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂x}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\frac{∂g}{∂x} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362159 13194139535702 true] [17592186362158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362160 13194139535702 true] [17592186362158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362161 13194139535702 true] [17592186362158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362162 13194139535702 true] [17592186362158 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362163 13194139535702 true] [17592186362158 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535702 true] [17592186362158 1041 "selection" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362158 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362163 13194139535702 true] [17592186362158 1110 #uuid "6e0b1c14-ccfb-5db5-aa5d-3a11009350e9" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362159 1034 "∂g,\\text{ }-Q,\\text{ }∂Q" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362159 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535702 true] [17592186362159 1111 #uuid "111d65f2-376d-5456-9f07-63ef6bd264a8" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362160 1034 "∂g,\\text{ }Q,\\text{ }∂z" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362160 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535702 true] [17592186362160 1111 #uuid "79bee6ea-c2d0-5ebd-850e-e267dc95b68e" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362161 1034 "∂g,\\text{ }-Q,\\text{ }∂z" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535702 true] [17592186362161 1111 #uuid "ba6d0d49-fa17-573a-a761-cdf2234d23ea" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362162 1034 "∂g,\\text{ }-Q,\\text{ }∂y" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535702 true] [17592186362162 1111 #uuid "ef7c9ca4-c7a4-5650-bcd4-3bed3109a217" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362163 1034 "∂g,\\text{ }Q,\\text{ }∂y" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535702 true] [17592186362163 1111 #uuid "bf1d4e7b-209b-5203-be60-bd097c1f0b6e" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362164 1017 #edb/ref 17592186362165 13194139535702 true] [17592186362164 1089 "q-161536" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362164 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535702 true] [17592186362164 1100 "Calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z={e}^{x}$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362164 1113 #uuid "1ba113f9-8e6f-5431-9993-fef9b213da77" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362164 1145 "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x})={e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x})=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the flux of $F$ through $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩{|}_{z={e}^{x}} \\\\  & =⟨{{y}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{x+{e}^{x}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{0}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨y,\\,x+z,\\,0⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y\\cdot ({e}^{x})-(x+{e}^{x})\\cdot 0+0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-y{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[-\\frac{{y}^{2}{e}^{x}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{[{e}^{x}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-1}-e}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362166 13194139535702 true] [17592186362165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362167 13194139535702 true] [17592186362165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362168 13194139535702 true] [17592186362165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362169 13194139535702 true] [17592186362165 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362170 13194139535702 true] [17592186362165 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535702 true] [17592186362165 1041 "selection" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362165 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362168 13194139535702 true] [17592186362165 1110 #uuid "056f196e-3bbc-50c0-89ba-8f81c9154689" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362166 1034 "-\\frac{5e+2{e}^{-1}}{4}" 13194139535702 true] [17592186362166 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535702 true] [17592186362166 1111 #uuid "b924de85-1175-5542-94c9-37664d8a7f51" 131941395